	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  problème de server]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=30702#p30702"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,<br />ça n&#039;a pas marché malheureusement, le serveur n&#039;a pas voulu démarrer en plus quand j&#039;ai voulu démarrer avec --single ça n&#039;a pas marché:<br />[root@localhost ~]# su - postgres<br />Last login: Fri Feb 14 17:47:56 CET 2020 on pts/0<br />-bash-4.2$ psql<br />psql: could not connect to server: Connection refused<br />&#160; &#160; Is the server running on host &quot;localhost&quot; (::1) and accepting<br />&#160; &#160; TCP/IP connections on port 5432?<br />could not connect to server: Connection refused<br />&#160; &#160; Is the server running on host &quot;localhost&quot; (127.0.0.1) and accepting<br />&#160; &#160; TCP/IP connections on port 5432?<br />-bash-4.2$ psql postgres<br />psql: could not connect to server: Connection refused<br />&#160; &#160; Is the server running on host &quot;localhost&quot; (::1) and accepting<br />&#160; &#160; TCP/IP connections on port 5432?<br />could not connect to server: Connection refused<br />&#160; &#160; Is the server running on host &quot;localhost&quot; (127.0.0.1) and accepting<br />&#160; &#160; TCP/IP connections on port 5432?<br />-bash-4.2$ pg_ctl -D postgres restart<br />pg_ctl: directory &quot;postgres&quot; does not exist<br />-bash-4.2$ pg_ctl -D postgres start<br />pg_ctl: directory &quot;postgres&quot; does not exist<br />-bash-4.2$ postgres --single<br />2020-02-17 07:41:35.938 GMT [3999] LOG:&#160; syntax error in file &quot;/var/lib/pgsql/10/data/postgresql.conf&quot; line 1, near token &quot;-&quot;<br />2020-02-17 07:41:35.938 GMT [3999] LOG:&#160; syntax error in file &quot;/var/lib/pgsql/10/data/postgresql.conf&quot; line 437, near token &quot;%&quot;<br />2020-02-17 07:41:35.938 GMT [3999] FATAL:&#160; configuration file &quot;/var/lib/pgsql/10/data/postgresql.conf&quot; contains errors<br />-bash-4.2$ cd $PGDATA<br />-bash-4.2$ vi postgresql.conf<br />-bash-4.2$ \q<br />bash: q: command not found...<br />-bash-4.2$ pg_ctl -D postgres restart<br />pg_ctl: directory &quot;postgres&quot; does not exist</p><p>==&gt; le pire pg_ctl n&#039;existe plus</p>]]></content>
